this one-byte message.  Clients such as
.B /dis/math/draw3ddev.dis
send
.B 3
before using the remaining letters.
.HP
.B C
.IR dstid [4]
.br
Write the draw3d capability mask to the first pixel of the 32-bit image
.IR dstid ,
least-significant byte first.  Bits 0 through 5 advertise matrices/state,
filled polygons, lines, points, sprites, and ellipses respectively.  Bit 6
advertises direct GPU rendering, bit 7 ordered GPU readback, bit 8 near-plane
clipping, and bit 9 software/Metal depth-order parity.  Clients should select
each optional path from this mask; the older
.B 3
probe remains for compatibility.
.HP
.B M
.IR which [1]
.IR m [16×4]
.br
